WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.038
No country had ever landed this close

2
00:00:02.038 --> 00:00:03.779
to the Moon's south pole.

3
00:00:03.779 --> 00:00:05.463
Until the twenty-third of August,

4
00:00:05.463 --> 00:00:06.959
2023.

5
00:00:07.359 --> 00:00:09.902
Chandrayaan-3 lifted off from Sriharikota on the

6
00:00:09.902 --> 00:00:10.749
fourteenth of July,

7
00:00:10.749 --> 00:00:12.628
on an LVM3 rocket.

8
00:00:13.028 --> 00:00:13.899
Forty days later,

9
00:00:13.899 --> 00:00:15.882
the Vikram lander touched down.

10
00:00:16.282 --> 00:00:18.581
India became the fourth country to soft-land

11
00:00:18.581 --> 00:00:19.626
on the Moon,

12
00:00:19.626 --> 00:00:21.969
and the first near its south pole.

13
00:00:22.369 --> 00:00:23.832
Why the south pole?

14
00:00:23.832 --> 00:00:26.049
Some craters there never see sunlight.

15
00:00:26.049 --> 00:00:27.870
They may hold water ice.

16
00:00:28.270 --> 00:00:30.337
Then the Pragyan rover rolled out.

17
00:00:30.337 --> 00:00:32.438
It drove about a hundred metres,

18
00:00:32.438 --> 00:00:34.607
and confirmed sulphur in the soil.

19
00:00:35.007 --> 00:00:36.505
Vikram even hopped:

20
00:00:36.505 --> 00:00:38.130
it lifted about forty centimetres,

21
00:00:38.130 --> 00:00:39.533
and landed again.

22
00:00:39.933 --> 00:00:41.674
The landing spot is called Shiv Shakti

23
00:00:41.674 --> 00:00:42.615
point.

24
00:00:42.615 --> 00:00:44.391
And the twenty-third of August is now

25
00:00:44.391 --> 00:00:45.806
National Space Day.

